        "description": "## GET /api/auth/profile\n\nRetrieves the authenticated user's profile information.\n\n### Authentication\n\nThis endpoint requires a valid **Bearer token** passed in the `Authorization` header. The token is referenced via the variable `{{json_web_token_0i1z}}`.\n\n### Notes\n\n> ⚠️ **Request Body:** A JSON body containing `email` and `password` is currently attached to this request. However, `GET` requests conventionally do not include a body — most servers and proxies will ignore it. If credentials are needed for authentication, they should be passed via the Bearer token (already configured) rather than in the request body. Consider removing the body or switching to a `POST` request if credential submission is intended.\n\n### Expected Response\n\nOn success, the server returns the profile data of the currently authenticated user.",
